' Listing 1 of Grogono's article (BYTE, July 1979, p. 206): square and
' triangular numbers computed by two mutually recursive macros.
'   S(n) = T(n) + T(n-1),  T(n) = (S(n-1) + 3n - 1) / 2,  S(1) = T(1) = 1
' Transcribed from the scan: the only changes are ^ for the printed up
' arrow, straight quotes, spacing and line breaks outside strings, and these
' comment lines. Strings are as printed (spaces inside strings are read
' from proportional type, so their exact count is approximate).
' The title has no "!" and the prompt no trailing space, so the title,
' the prompt and the answer run together on one line of output.
"SQUARE AND TRIANGULAR NUMBERS"
( "ENTER A NUMBER" N ? = N. ^
  "S(" N. ! ") = " #S,N.; !
  "   T(" N. ! ") = " #T,N.; ! "!" )

$S %A 1 - [ #T,%A; #T,%A 1 -; + @ ] 1 @
$T %A 1 - [ #S,%A 1 -; 3 %A * 1 - + 2 / @ ] 1 @
$$
